WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:06.029
On its opening weekend, the Stephen King adaptation
It broke multiple box-office records when

00:00:06.029 --> 00:00:12.770
it pulled in $123 million — the biggest-ever
September opening for a film, horror or otherwise.

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:17.100
We can't ignore the impressive performances
from the young cast, and, of course, the film's

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.960
terrifying demon clown.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:22.689
Let's take a closer look at this group of
fictional misfits, and the talented young

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:26.250
actors who brought their characters to life
on the big screen.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.220
Jaeden Lieberher

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:33.520
Before landing a starring role in It as Bill
Denbrough, actor Jaeden Lieberher started

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.810
his acting career with appearances in commercial
spots as a talented eight-year-old with no

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:39.060
professional training.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:43.500
He was soon being cast in films, appearing
in St. Vincent with Bill Murray, Playing It

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:49.070
Cool, and Aloha before getting his first starring
role in the 2016 science fiction film Midnight

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:50.070
Special.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:54.100
You may also recognize Lieberher from his
recurring role as Johnny Masters in the Showtime

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.660
period drama series Masters of Sex.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.620
Jackson Robert Scott

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:04.140
Georgie Denbrough is Bill's cheerful and innocent
seven-year-old younger brother.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:09.400
And, well, we all know what happens to Georgie.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:14.190
At only eight years old, Jackson Robert Scott's
budding acting career is just beginning.

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:18.680
Before appearing as Georgie in It, he also
had single-episode roles in the television

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:24.680
shows Criminal Minds in 2015 and Fear the
Walking Dead in 2017.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:26.000
Sophia Lillis

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:31.230
As the sole female in the Losers' Club, Bev
Marsh is an obvious target for the boys' adolescent

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:36.450
crushes, and every member of the club harbors
feelings for her at one point or another.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:40.800
Sophia Lillis started off her acting career
with appearances in several small-budget shorts

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.810
and feature films, including A Midsummer Night's
Dream, 37, and The Garden.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:50.479
In addition to It, you can spot her this year
in a role as the younger version of the lead

00:01:50.479 --> 00:01:55.170
character in an episode of the upcoming HBO
series Sharp Objects.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.940
Jeremy Ray Taylor

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:01.620
Ben Hanscom is smart and extremely talented
when it comes to inventing and engineering,

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:05.920
but because of his weight, he's frequently
targeted by town bully Henry Bowers and his

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.729
gang of cronies.

00:02:07.729 --> 00:02:13.120
Before being bullied in It, Jeremy Ray Taylor
portrayed a bully himself in the 2015 superhero

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:14.200
movie Ant-Man.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:20.040
He's also had parts in 42, Good Behavior,
and Alvin and the Chipmunks: The Road Chip.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:21.540
Finn Wolfhard

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:27.110
Richie Tozier has a tendency to chatter incessantly,
and an overwhelming amount of bravado for

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:32.690
his age, alongside a considerable vocabulary
of curse words at his disposal — which duly

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:35.530
earns him the nickname "Trashmouth."

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:40.921
Of all the Losers' Club cast, Finn Wolfhard
is perhaps the most easily recognizable, due

00:02:40.921 --> 00:02:45.459
to his leading role as Mike Wheeler in the
hit Netflix series Stranger Things.

00:02:45.459 --> 00:02:49.940
In addition to that role, Wolfhard has also
appeared in The 100 and Supernatural, as well

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:54.790
as directing and starring in the music video
for the song "Sonora" from Spendtime Palace.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:58.850
His next project will be as the voice of the
primary "Player" character in the upcoming

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:02.550
Netflix animated series Carmen Sandiego.

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.010
Jack Dylan Grazer

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:08.820
Where Richie is filled with bravado and appears
fearless, Eddie seems terrified of everything.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.489
"Have you ever heard of a staph infection?"

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:12.830
"Oh I'll show you a staph infection."

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:17.819
Due to his overbearing mother, Eddie is a
chronic hypochondriac, afraid of his own shadow

00:03:17.819 --> 00:03:22.150
and clutching his asthma inhaler like a holy
relic to ward off evil.

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:26.220
As the nephew of Hollywood producer Brian
Grazer, Jack Dylan Grazer's talents run in

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.220
the family.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:31.650
He made his first appearance in 2014 on an
episode of The Greatest Event in Television

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:33.930
History, followed by roles in Comedy Bang!

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:37.790
Bang!, Tales of Halloween, and Scales: Mermaids
Are Real.

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:42.820
Following It, Grazer can be seen in the CBS
comedy series Me, Myself &amp; I.

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.459
Chosen Jacobs

00:03:44.459 --> 00:03:48.400
Mike serves as an unofficial "historian" for
the group — helping them connect the dots

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:53.650
between events in Derry's past, like the fire
at the Black Spot, the Bradley Gang shootout,

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:55.870
and the mass murder at the Silver Dollar.

00:03:55.870 --> 00:04:00.459
Chosen Jacobs started his career as a musician
in Atlanta, and after moving to California,

00:04:00.459 --> 00:04:04.510
he landed his first acting role at age 13
in a commercial for Hot Wheels.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:08.989
After being cast as Will Grover in the CBS
police drama series Hawaii Five-0, he landed

00:04:08.989 --> 00:04:13.769
his breakout role as Mike Hanlon in It with
only a single audition.

00:04:13.769 --> 00:04:15.800
Wyatt Oleff

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:20.209
Stan is a bit eccentric, and his Jewish heritage
paired with his bird-calling hobby make him

00:04:20.209 --> 00:04:22.550
a natural target for Henry Bowers and his
gang.

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:27.259
A pragmatic and logical boy, Stan's sound
reasoning helps the Losers' Club on more than

00:04:27.259 --> 00:04:28.430
one occasion.

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:32.759
Of all the Losers' Club cast, Wyatt Oleff
has the longest list of acting credits, with

00:04:32.759 --> 00:04:34.550
roles going back to 2012.

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:39.120
He's appeared in television shows like Once
Upon a Time, Shake It Up!, and Scorpion, and

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:42.681
you might recognize him for his role as a
young Peter Quill in both Guardians of the

00:04:42.681 --> 00:04:44.629
Galaxy films.

00:04:44.629 --> 00:04:45.800
Nicholas Hamilton

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:50.900
Henry Bowers leads a gang of high school kids
on a campaign of torment aimed at various

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:55.509
members of the Losers' Club — Ben Hanscom
and Mike Hanlon in particular.

00:04:55.509 --> 00:04:57.169
It's all downhill from there.

00:04:57.169 --> 00:05:01.580
It wasn't the only Stephen King adaptation
to feature Australian actor Nicholas Hamilton

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:02.580
in 2017.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:07.599
He also appeared as Lucas Hanson in The Dark
Tower, and he's racked up an impressive list

00:05:07.599 --> 00:05:12.430
of roles in his short acting career, including
parts in the Australian television series

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:17.360
Wanted, the feature film Strangerland, and
Captain Fantastic with Viggo Mortensen.

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:18.749
Owen Teague

00:05:18.749 --> 00:05:23.169
Patrick Hockstetter is a psychopathic high
schooler who likes to lock small animals inside

00:05:23.169 --> 00:05:27.949
an abandoned refrigerator until they die,
which makes him a perfect fit for Henry Bowers'

00:05:27.949 --> 00:05:28.949
gang.

00:05:28.949 --> 00:05:32.129
Owen Teague made quite a few appearances in
television shows and films before landing

00:05:32.129 --> 00:05:34.060
the part of the psychopathic Patrick.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:38.589
You may recognize him as the young version
of Walt Disney in the 2015 film Walt Before

00:05:38.589 --> 00:05:43.289
Mickey, from other movies like Echoes of War,
or the 2016 adaptation of another Stephen

00:05:43.289 --> 00:05:48.270
King tale, Cell. Additionally, Teague played
the role of Nolan Rayburn in over twenty episodes

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:51.409
of the Netflix original thriller series Bloodline.

00:05:51.409 --> 00:05:52.659
Jake Sim

00:05:52.659 --> 00:05:57.110
Although Reginald "Belch" Huggins isn't the
brightest crayon in the box, his size, strength,

00:05:57.110 --> 00:06:01.060
and loyalty makes him a valuable asset to
Henry Bowers' crew.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:05.849
Jake Sim's acting career really got going
in 2010 when he landed a voice role as Tommy

00:06:05.849 --> 00:06:07.860
Tibble, in the animated series Arthur.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:12.119
He also provided his voice talent to another
animated children's' show, Stella and Sam,

00:06:12.119 --> 00:06:13.189
in 2013.

00:06:13.189 --> 00:06:17.849
Onscreen, Sim has had roles in several other
shows, including The Amazing Gayl Pile, and

00:06:17.849 --> 00:06:20.100
Raising Expectations.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:21.669
Bill Skarsgård

00:06:21.669 --> 00:06:27.409
At age 27, Bill Skarsgård is definitely not
one of the "kids" from It, but the terror

00:06:27.409 --> 00:06:32.289
and suspense of the movie rests squarely on
his colorful shoulders as Pennywise.

00:06:32.289 --> 00:06:37.319
Before taking on the role that Tim Curry made
famous in 1990, Swedish actor Bill Skarsgård

00:06:37.319 --> 00:06:41.379
appeared in a number of films and television
shows, starting with roles in primarily Swedish

00:06:41.379 --> 00:06:46.129
productions like Simple Simon before transitioning
to English-language feature films and shows

00:06:46.129 --> 00:06:49.500
like Hemlock Grove, Atomic Blonde, and Allegiant.

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:54.219
Although he'll presumably be back for the
sequel, Skarsgård's next project is a recurring

00:06:54.219 --> 00:06:58.479
role in the upcoming Hulu original series
Castle Rock — also based on the works of

00:06:58.479 --> 00:06:59.479
Stephen King.

00:06:59.479 --> 00:07:00.539
Thanks for watching!

00:07:00.539 --> 00:07:02.919
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:02.919 --> 00:07:04.779
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

